tion and a bruised GOP primary in which gun YouTuber Brandon Herrera forced a runoff. The district leans Republican by about seven points, and the national climate favors the GOP this cycle, giving Herrera a structural edge despite his controversial comments about Nazi weapons and women that have drawn sustained negative coverage.\n\nDemocrat Katy Padilla Stout has out-raised expectations and national Democrats have added the district to their target list, but she trails in money on hand and lacks outside spending so far. Markets price the Republican at roughly 60 percent, and expert raters mostly call the race Likely or Lean Republican. The expected outcome is a Republican hold by mid-single digits, with meaningful uncertainty given the sparse polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2302, "margin": -5.0}]}